    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0189" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d139-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-18">November 18, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For the President from Secretary Hull.</p>
                <p>Kirk thinks<anchor n="2" xml:id="d139-f2"/> it would be appropriate for you to
                    send message to King Farouk to wish him recovery from recent motor accident
                    which resulted in slight injury to pelvis and minor bruises.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d139-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d139-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d139-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the White House Map Room to Greer at Oran, apparently via military
                    channels, November 19, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d139-f2" n="2" xml:id="d139-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 2116, November 17, 1943, from the Legation at Cairo; not printed
                    herein.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d139-f3" n="3" xml:id="d139-f3-content">
                <p>For Roosevelt’s message of November 20, 1943, to Farouk, based on this
                    suggestion, see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg101">p.
                        101</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
